WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.320
CI/CD turns patching into a repeatable flow.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.460
Dependency-update tools can propose new base images or library versions,

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.200
but proposals still need ownership, review, and testing.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:16.060
Unreviewed automation can introduce incompatible code, untrusted artifacts,

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.240
or changes that bypass risk decisions.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:24.580
Pipeline scans evaluate source dependencies, build inputs, and completed images.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.520
Policy gates enforce defined requirements before promotion, such as approved base images,

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:34.060
acceptable vulnerability posture, successful tests, required SBOMs,

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.960
or reviewed exceptions.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.980
Build provenance records how an artifact was created.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.640
Signing associates an approved identity with the image digest,

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.420
while verification helps registries and clusters reject artifacts that do not meet policy.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.920
Protect signing keys, build identities, and pipeline credentials as high-value assets.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:57.380
Registry controls limit who can push, retag, delete, and pull images.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:03.920
Retain immutable digests, scanning results, SBOMs, signatures, and lifecycle records.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.540
Promotion should move the same tested artifact through environments instead of rebuilding

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.920
unrelated copies for each stage.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:14.020
Automation should surface decisions rather than hide them.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.920
Clear reports explain the changed dependency, risk addressed, tests run, policy result,

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:22.460
approver, and destination.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:27.560
Exceptions should be explicit, time-limited, and visible to later promotion steps.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.420
Measure pipeline reliability as well as speed.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:35.760
Failed updates, stale pull requests, bypassed gates, unsigned images,

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:40.060
and differences between approved and deployed digests reveal process weakness.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:45.720
Good automation shortens remediation while preserving evidence, separation of duties,

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:47.460
and controlled release.
